    "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#AmpereTurn",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The `ampere-turn` was the MKS unit of magnetomotive force (MMF), represented by a direct current of one ampere flowing in a single-turn loop in a vacuum. \"Turns\" refers to the winding number of an electrical conductor comprising an inductor. The ampere-turn was replaced by the SI unit, ampere.\n\n-- QUDT"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
