  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/battgpt/kg#CrystalStructure",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Crystallographic structural representation describing the periodic arrangement, unit cell, symmetry, and atomic sites of a material. Explicitly anchored under owl:Thing (v0.3.0) for consistency with its sibling local classes (Site, UnitCell, Species, CrystalBond); no single class in EMMO core, EMMO domain-battery, EMMO domain-electrochemistry, or EMMO domain-chemical-substance cleanly captures 'the crystallographic structure of a substance', and EMMO's own domain-crystallography ontology remains an explicitly work-in-progress v0.1.0 draft not imported here, so this is left as a standalone local root rather than force-fit under an unstable upstream branch."
      }
    ],
