      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Specific heat capacity - The heat required to raise unit mass of a substance by unit temperature interval under specified conditions, such as constant pressure: usually measured in joules per kelvin per kilogram. Symbol c_p (for constant pressure) Also called specific heat.\n\n-- QUDT"
      }
    ]
