    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The \"Newton\" is the SI unit of force. A force of one newton will accelerate a mass of one kilogram at the rate of one meter per second per second. The newton is named for Isaac Newton (1642-1727), the British mathematician, physicist, and natural philosopher. He was the first person to understand clearly the relationship between force (F), mass (m), and acceleration (a) expressed by the formula F = m·a.\n\n-- QUDT"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c84c6752_6d64_48cc_9500_e54a3c34898d": [
