    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The Planck energy divided by the Planck time is the Planck power Pₚ , equal to about 3.62831 × 10⁵² W. This is an extremely large unit; even gamma-ray bursts, the most luminous phenomena known, have output on the order of 1 × 10⁴⁵ W, less than one ten-millionth of the Planck power.\n\n-- QUDT"
      }
    ],
