        "@value": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Graviton"
      }
    ]
  },
  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#Dalton",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The unified atomic mass unit (symbol: μ) or dalton (symbol: Da) is a unit that is used for indicating mass on an atomic or molecular scale. It is defined as one twelfth of the rest mass of an unbound atom of carbon-12 in its nuclear and electronic ground state, and has a value of 1.660538782(83) × 10⁻²⁷ kg. One Da is approximately equal to the mass of one proton or one neutron. The CIPM have categorised it as a \"non-SI unit whose values in SI units must be obtained experimentally\".\n\n-- QUDT"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "One dalton is defined as one twelfth of the mass of an unbound neutral atom of carbon-12 in its nuclear and electronic ground state."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/units/siacceptedspecialunits#"
      },
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "http://qudt.org/2.1/vocab/unit"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
