  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_64c72d00_7582_44ea_a0b5_3a14e50acc36",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The General Definition of Information (GDI) can be used to define the concept of information.\n(GDI) a is an instance of information, understood as semantic content, if and only if:\n  GDI.l) a consists of n data, for n > 1;\n  GDI.2) the data are well formed;\n  GDI.3) the well-formed data are meaningful.\n\nIn the EMMO conceptualisation, well-formed data are data with a specific syntactic structure (symbolic and reductionistic modules), while meaningful data are data that are part of a semiotic interpretation process that declares what the data are about (semiotic module)."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information is data with a meaning (semiotic sign)."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/information#"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_b21a56ed_f969_4612_a6ec_cb7766f7f31d"
      },
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_3e7add3d_e6ed_489a_a796_8e31fef9b490"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#equivalentClass": [
      {
        "@id": "_:n6a0b4d77db1d4bb4a28be148935c0b69b4818"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The General Definition of Information (GDI) can be used to define the concept of information.\n(GDI) a is an instance of information, understood as semantic content, if and only if:\n  GDI.l) a consists of n data, for n > 1;\n  GDI.2) the data are well formed;\n  GDI.3) the well-formed data are meaningful.\n\nIn the EMMO conceptualisation, well-formed data are data with a specific syntactic structure (symbolic and reductionistic modules), while meaningful data are data that are part of a semiotic interpretation process that declares what the data are about (semiotic module)."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Information is data with a meaning (semiotic sign)."
      }
    ]
  },
