  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_38b579de_4331_40e0_803d_09efa298e726",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The class of individuals standing for causally convex interacting systems."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "It is natural to define entities made or more than one smaller parts as object according to some unity criteria. One of the most general one applicable to causal interacting systems is to ask that all the quantum parts of the system are part of elementaries whose paths start and end within the entitiy. We call this causal convexity. In other words, causal convexity excludes all quantums that leave the system (no more interacting), or that are not yet part of it (not yet interacting).\nSo, a photon leaving a body is not part of a convex system, while a real photon that is the carrier of clasical electromagnetic interaction between two molecular parts of the body, is part of the convex body.\nA physical phenomenon is defined as a causally non-convex interacting system, complement of causally convex interacting system."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo/disciplines/chemistry#"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "PhysicalObject"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_09f0ac34_c349_46b5_acf0_0edeae52cca1"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#disjointWith": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_5cc4e111_3eb1_44a3_9369_5af3846cf605"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "PhysicalObject"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "It is natural to define entities made or more than one smaller parts as object according to some unity criteria. One of the most general one applicable to causal interacting systems is to ask that all the quantum parts of the system are part of elementaries whose paths start and end within the entitiy. We call this causal convexity. In other words, causal convexity excludes all quantums that leave the system (no more interacting), or that are not yet part of it (not yet interacting).\nSo, a photon leaving a body is not part of a convex system, while a real photon that is the carrier of clasical electromagnetic interaction between two molecular parts of the body, is part of the convex body.\nA physical phenomenon is defined as a causally non-convex interacting system, complement of causally convex interacting system."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "DisjointUnionOf: CompositePhysicalObject, BondedObject"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The class of individuals standing for causally convex interacting systems."
      }
    ]
  },
