  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_9e49caad_b29e_4cf1_9be4_80419fd1e45c",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An array is a datatype representing an ordered collection of elements (or values) that can be accessed by indexes. Arrays have an analog mathematical counterpart in vectors and matrixes, but are separate concepts. Arrays may be multidimensional."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo/reference/symbolic#"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ArrayData"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_70bbb94e_2ca7_4d73_ba01_6397f134d172"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "ArrayData"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_31252f35_c767_4b97_a877_1235076c3e13": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An array is a datatype representing an ordered collection of elements (or values) that can be accessed by indexes. Arrays have an analog mathematical counterpart in vectors and matrixes, but are separate concepts. Arrays may be multidimensional."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "SubClassOf: hasScalarData some ScalarData"
      },
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "SubClassOf: hasSpatialTile some SymbolicData"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In the EMMO we use the following JSON based syntax to represent arrays:\n- mono-dimensional array [v1,v2,...,vn] (vector)\n- bi-dimensional array [[v1,v2,...,vn],[w1,w2,...,2n]] (matrix)\nThis notation can be extended to multidimensional arrays."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The structure of an array is expressed mereologically. It consists of a set of equally sized tiles.\nThe tiles of an n-dimensional array are (n-1) dimensional arrays. The tiles of an (n-1)-dimensional array are (n-2) dimensional arrays, and so forth down to 1-dimensional arrays (vectors), whos tiles are scalar data."
      }
    ]
  },
