        "@value": "SubProcess"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_846b637b_7b12_47a1_9430_0274b2f588ac"
      },
      {
        "@id": "_:n6a0b4d77db1d4bb4a28be148935c0b69b3702"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Breathing is a subprocess of living for a human being."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "SubProcess"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A process which is a spatial part of another process."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In the EMMO the relation of participation to a process falls under mereotopology.\n\nSince topological connection means causality, then the only way for a real world object to participate to a process is to be a part of it."
      }
    ]
  },
