      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Vector quantity giving the rate of change of a position vector.\n\n-- ISO 80000-3"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The velocity depends on the choice of the reference frame. Proper transformation between frames must be used: Galilean for non-relativistic description, Lorentzian for relativistic description.\n\n-- IEC, note 2"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "The velocity is related to a point described by its position vector. The point may localize a particle, or be attached to any other object such as a body or a wave.\n\n-- IEC, note 1"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
