      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "\"StatMHO\" is the unit of conductance, admittance, and susceptance in the C.G.S e.s.u system of units. One statmho is the conductance between two points in a conductor when a constant potential difference of 1 statvolt applied between the points produces in the conductor a current of 1 statampere, the conductor not being the source of any electromotive force, approximately 1.1126 × 10⁻¹² mho.\n\n-- QUDT"
      }
    ]
  },
