  {
    "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_d7788d1a_020d_4c78_85a1_13563fcec168",
    "@type": [
      "http://www.w3.org/2002/07/owl#Class"
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A sign that stands for an object by resembling or imitating it, in shape, function or by sharing a similar logical structure."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo/perspectives/semiotics#"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#label": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Icon"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#subClassOf": [
      {
        "@id": "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_4a2bf359_c47b_4aa3_9811_b59c3e1dac1e"
      },
      {
        "@id": "_:n6a0b4d77db1d4bb4a28be148935c0b69b4708"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#altLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Simulacrum"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Model"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#example": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A picture that reproduces the aspect of a person."
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "An equation that reproduces the logical connection of the properties of a physical entity."
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2004/02/skos/core#prefLabel": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "Icon"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_8a137e9f_579c_4e28_baca_e8980eb0c3db": [
      {
        "@type": "http://www.w3.org/2001/XMLSchema#string",
        "@value": "EquivalentTo: AnalogicalIcon or ResemblanceIcon or FunctionalIcon"
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_967080e5_2f42_4eb2_a3a9_c58143e835f9": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "A sign that stands for an object by resembling or imitating it, in shape, function or by sharing a similar logical structure."
      }
    ],
    "https://w3id.org/emmo#EMMO_c7b62dd7_063a_4c2a_8504_42f7264ba83f": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In Peirce semiotics three subtypes of icon are possible:\n(a) the image, which depends on a simple quality (e.g. picture)\n(b) the diagram, whose internal relations, mainly dyadic or so taken, represent by analogy the relations in something (e.g. math formula, geometric flowchart)\n(c) the metaphor, which represents the representative character of a sign by representing a parallelism in something else\n[Wikipedia]"
      },
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "If object and sign belongs to the same class, then the sign is fuctional, diagrammatic and resemblance.\nFor example, when a Boeing 747 is used as a sign for another Boeing 747."
      }
    ]
  },
