    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#comment": [
      {
        "@language": "en",
        "@value": "In physics, the unit of energy in the system of natural units known as Planck units is called the Planck energy, denoted by Eₚ. Eₚ is a derived, as opposed to basic, Planck unit. An equivalent definition is: Eₚ = ℏ / tₚ where tₚ is the Planck time. Also: Eₚ = mₚ c² where mₚ is the Planck mass.\n\n-- QUDT"
      }
    ],
    "http://www.w3.org/2000/01/rdf-schema#isDefinedBy": [
